WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.340
Clear messages, voice notes, files and Status.

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:08.400
This is the video for module two of WhatsApp for Communication and Business.

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:16.440
Text messages are still the heart of WhatsApp. A clear message shows respect and, in business, wins trust.

4
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:23.420
Voice notes and calls save time, but a five-minute voice note can frustrate a busy customer.

5
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:30.500
Each kind of file has a best way to send it, to keep pictures sharp and your bundle under control.

6
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:39.110
And Status lets you post updates that disappear after 24 hours. Many traders call it their free shop window.

7
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:49.210
In a busy chat, yes can mean anything. Swipe a message to the right to reply to it. The original appears in a small box above your answer.

8
00:00:50.460 --> 00:01:00.570
Put a star before and after a word to make it bold. Start a line with a dash and a space to make a list. Keep it light. A whole message in bold feels like shouting.

9
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:10.230
Typed the wrong account number? Press and hold, and tap Edit. You can edit for up to 15 minutes, so nobody pays into the wrong account.

10
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:20.140
Text has no tone of voice, so Ok can sound cold. Start with a greeting, use the person's name, and end with a clear next step.

11
00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:29.710
Here is a worked example. Amaka sells small chops in Port Harcourt. A customer asks for 50 packs for a birthday on Saturday.

12
00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.010
Amaka swipes right on the order, so her reply sits under it, and types Order confirmed in bold.

13
00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:50.850
Then a dash list. 50 packs at 1,500 naira each. Delivery Saturday at 11am. And please pay 50 percent, that is 37,500 naira, to confirm.

14
00:01:52.100 --> 00:02:00.100
The total, 75,000 naira, is in bold. The customer has no questions, and the deposit arrives within the hour.

15
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:09.520
Put account numbers, prices, addresses and dates in text. People can copy them, and nobody can search inside a voice note.

16
00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:20.310
Hold the microphone to record, and slide up to lock for a longer note. Plan first: who you are, what you need, the next step. Try to keep it under a minute.

17
00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:31.260
For a sensitive matter, call. To show a product, use a video call. Zainab the tailor showed her customer a wedding outfit this way, then confirmed the change in text.

18
00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:38.890
WhatsApp shrinks photos to save data. For everyday pictures to family, standard quality is fine.

19
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:47.860
For a product photo, tap the HD button before sending. HD uses more data, so keep it for pictures that sell.

20
00:02:49.110 --> 00:03:02.510
Send price lists, invoices and scans as a Document. It arrives exactly as it left your phone. Esther, a decorator in Enugu, sends her quotes as a named PDF, which the client can print.

21
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:11.840
A contact sees your status only if you saved their number and they saved yours. That is why traders say, please save my number.

22
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:26.530
Tola sells Ankara dresses in Akure to about 600 saved contacts. On Monday she posts HD photos of new dresses with the price and sizes in the caption, and the words Reply to order.

23
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:32.860
On Wednesday she posts a happy customer's message, with permission and the name hidden.

24
00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:38.140
On Friday, last 3 pieces at this price, offer ends Saturday.

25
00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:47.220
She replies to every status reply within an hour. Replies arrive with the photo attached, so she knows which dress they mean.

26
00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.390
But never post your children's school name, your travel plans, or piles of cash.

27
00:03:53.640 --> 00:04:05.950
Forwarded many times is a warning sign. Messages about free grants, jobs or bank closures are very often false, and ones that ask for your BVN or bank details are scams.

28
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:15.930
So ask: who wrote it, is there a date, can I confirm it, could it harm? And never send your card PIN, OTP or card details on WhatsApp.

29
00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:32.830
To remember. Reply to the exact message and bold the key line. Put key numbers in text. Use HD for products and Document for PDFs. Post a few strong status updates, each with one action. And check before you forward.

30
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:45.070
Now practise on your own phone. Send yourself a formatted message, record a voice note under 60 seconds, send a PDF as a Document, and post two status updates.

31
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.580
Then continue with the lessons below.
